WEBVTT

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.500
It sure is freezing today!

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.130
The downtown area got down to 37 degrees at 6:00 this morning.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.990
It looks like it's finally that time of year where you need a coat to step outside.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.660
And now, the weather for the Kanto region.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.340
Today, the Kanto region is covered by a winter pressure system...

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.640
I'm sorry, I must have woken you up.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:52.010
Good morning. You're up early, Touko.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.710
Most female office workers are up at this hour.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.320
I guess people in Italy all get up late.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.450
I wouldn't say that.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.280
I thought all nuns were early risers, but I guess that's not true.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.850
Here's your key.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.130
I need to get going, so lock up when you leave, okay?

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.970
I made coffee for you. Should I have?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.910
No, it's all right. I used to drink it a lot.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.080
If you have any trouble, give me a call whenever.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.410
That's what your boss told me to tell you.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.250
Boss...?

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.950
Don't tell me that you don't know who that is.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.920
I think I do. Maybe.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.450
Things have been really hectic.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.890
Well, that's true...

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.330
Just take your time and get settled in.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.830
Moments ago, the lawsuit against Mr. Kazuya Misawa,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.170
...owner of an import retail business, was withdrawn.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.780
Mr. Misawa has just come out!

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.420
Mr. Misawa! First of all, how do you feel right now?

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.700
Murder by Curse!
Breaking News!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.910
I would like to thank everyone who has stood by me.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.410
I also feel tremendous anger toward the foolish behavior of the police.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.560
This means that you will be able to move forward with the contract...

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.550
...with a well-known American company that's been on hold pending this verdict, doesn't it?

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.860
That means nothing to me.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.700
I just wanted to tell everyone that there is only one truth.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.030
The truth will always...

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.750
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:39.480
...the instant I look away.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.620
I just kept counting...

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:50.060
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:57.430
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:03.370
In this time that seems so dry,

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:08.480
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:14.340
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.390
...and tears them to pieces.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:27.060
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:34.890
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.170
Let's see...

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.710
Good morning. I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.310
Oh, no, that's all right. Good morning.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.180
Kazuya Misawa.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.760
The media pressure made it impossible to continue the court case.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.830
I thought it would be all right for him to be tried under the judicial system, but...

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.260
We'll be handling him, then?

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.170
Right.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.070
What's this about?

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.280
How could you not know?!

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.910
No, you weren't in Japan at the time, so it's only natural that you're unfamiliar with the case.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.280
Michael.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.150
Yeah.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.090
Right now, I am outside the district courthouse...

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.510
Mr. Misawa, what are your feelings right now?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.060
I would like to thank everyone who has stood by me.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.130
I also feel...

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.120
That's from this morning...

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.390
Okay, here's the stuff from before you arrived.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.540
This is our target, Kazuya Misawa. Age, 28.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.530
He's a suspect in the murder of his business partner.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.370
He thinks he's a movie star...

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.910
The victim was Yukihiro Watanabe. Age, 32.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.210
Apparently, he and Misawa were never on very good terms.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.750
Come off it, he's not crying.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.590
Killing someone with a curse? It's preposterous!

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.460
The crime occurred in an office of a building owned by Misawa.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.620
Cause of death was bleeding resulting from massive trauma to multiple organs.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.300
In response to police questioning, witnesses claim that Misawa...

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.320
...killed the victim with a curse, and that he never laid a finger on him.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.110
Even the coroner's report stated that the only possible conclusion...

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.010
...was that some powerful force was applied from inside the body.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.580
At this point, the data usually finds its way to the STN-J,

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.480
...and we get put in charge of the case.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:56.950
But this time, the detective in charge added a little fiction to the report.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:58.780
Fiction?

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.020
The case would never hold up if "curse" were listed under Cause of Death.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.490
Of course, the DA would never allow such a case to go to court.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.000
Are you an idiot?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.660
In other words, the generally accepted view is that witch powers don't exist.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.100
I see...

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.900
"I see"? You're starting to get on my nerves, you know that?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.140
Now that he knows the law can't touch his powers,

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.400
his activity will most likely escalate.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.580
We'll sneak past the eyes of the media and look for an opportunity to capture him.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.780
Sakaki, Karasuma. Do some digging around his workplace.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.750
Michael and I will look into his private life.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.250
- Sure.
- Roger.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.040
Father Juliano is doing well, I trust?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.050
You know the father?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.750
I've met him before back at Solomon.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.750
It's been well over a decade now...

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:18.720
Juliano is doing well, but his powers seem to have diminished.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.030
Oh, really?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.780
I realize that our methods may differ slightly from those at headquarters.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.450
Yes, quite a bit.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.380
But we have our own way of doing things.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.420
I expect you to abide by them.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.680
You mean how you don't kill witches?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.620
I'm sure it may seem odd to you,

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.620
but we've developed a system that captures them without killing them.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.330
Orbo?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.350
That's right.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.300
Orbo may have its downside of weakening our hunter's powers,

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.400
but it has the effect of preventing the target's powers from directly affecting our bodies.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:01.830
I'm sure a hunter of your caliber won't feel the need to use it,

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.410
...but bear in mind that we want to capture them, not kill them.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:07.710
Yes, sir. But...

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.520
Orbo is disgusting, so I won't be using it.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.090
I see...

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:18.390
All right, then, stick with this man here for now and get to know how things work around here.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.660
You're dismissed.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.960
Yes, sir.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.140
What do you think?

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.740
It seems to me that she has no interest in Orbo whatsoever.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.890
I don't know what they're up to back at headquarters.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.660
But be on your guard.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:57.330
You're dismissed.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.300
Yes, sir.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.840
Oh, could you come here a minute? Yeah, you... Um...

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.550
Robin-chan?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.910
I'm sorry, but could you bring me some tea?

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.350
I have your tea right here, Chief.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.590
Oh, sorry about that, Hattori.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.120
And Robin-chan, about your desk...

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:30.930
It's over there.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.000
Yes?

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.270
We finally got a sweet young thing in here,

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.640
but I won't be able to see her over there from my desk!

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:42.980
Robin-chan, if you ever need help with anything, feel free to come to me for help.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:46.820
Chief, about this "Robin-chan" stuff...

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:47.950
Is that a problem?

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.850
Well, not exactly, but...

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.990
Just using someone's first name seems a little strange, though.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.250
Chief, about this receipt from Snack Pub Komadori...

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.990
Now, I realize you said it was a business expense, but...

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.360
Can't you do something about it?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.700
Don't let him get to you.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.430
The Chief is always like that.

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.670
Just pretend that he's part of the furniture.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.630
You'll get used to how we do things around here really soon.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.900
See ya, Robin.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:19.910
I'll come with you.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.810
You ought to wait for orders from Amon.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:25.710
Until then, you should stay here with Michael and mind the fort.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.490
It would be a good idea to look over the case information to pass the time.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.850
Hey, where do you think you're going?

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.450
Out to do a little shopping.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:34.660
See ya!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.730
Geez...

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:01.660
Sorry.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:08.790
What do you suppose this is?

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:10.790
A church.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.630
You took this picture?

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.300
No, that was taken by the lead detective.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.870
Geez, analog people are terrible at collating information...

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.180
Actually, that material there hasn't been filed yet.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.740
Look through the stuff over here.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.400
Sorry. I'll leave them here.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.450
Where's Amon?

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.510
I think he left already.

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:52.000
A few people in the office witnessed the quarrel between the victim and the suspect,

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.100
...but nobody saw the quarrel from beginning to end.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:02.850
However, right after one witness saw Misawa shout, "I'll curse you to death!"...

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.580
Stop reading out loud, okay?

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:06.520
Sorry.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.960
"I'll curse you to death"...

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:27.130
- The body...
- The body...

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.070
What happened to it?

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.080
This isn't written down anywhere,

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:42.550
...but the coroner who did the autopsy said the internal organs had been twisted off.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.690
The police covered that up,

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.460
and arrested him on charges of beating the victim to death with a blunt object.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.370
In the past, Misawa has been investigated...

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.630
...for assault and for destruction of property on several occasions.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.100
But they were never able to arrest him due to lack of evidence.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.370
So they wanted to make sure that this murder charge would stick.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:09.050
In the end, the detective fabricated the report so he could arrest Misawa.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.950
In other words... That was the piece of fiction.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.450
Stop thinking out loud, okay?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.790
But it's true, right?

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:38.750
Hi, Amon.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.440
I just got some intel that the media doesn't have yet.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.580
He'll be getting married soon.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.950
The fiancée  is the daughter of a client, so that must have worked out nicely for him.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.990
The press hasn't caught wind of it,

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.550
...so the wedding preparations must be going on under tight wraps.

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.000
Wait a minute!

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.230
That picture.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.560
The one from before!

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.670
The detective?

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.730
Yeah... The detective found out.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.970
He had a picture of the chapel and some info on it.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.200
Michael.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.200
I already sent Karasuma and Sakaki to contact the fiancée.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.950
Dig up all you can on the chapel,

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.040
...and just in case, find out where that detective is.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.210
Okay, I'll get on it right away.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.520
Thanks.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.350
What should l...?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.190
This is it.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.090
She's being tricked.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.530
That woman is being tricked...

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:38.760
They got engaged... And he's not even human.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.650
That's the fiancée.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.280
She's pretty hot.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:57.420
On the outside.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.690
Nice timing, Michael!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.600
Here.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:04.760
I'm going in.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:06.500
Good luck.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.200
Excuse me. You must be Miss Nakamoto.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:15.830
I'm with TN Television. Could I have a moment of your time?

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:17.180
What is it?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.770
You'll be getting married to Mr. Misawa soon, right?

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:25.140
We'd like to get exclusive rights to cover the ceremony.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:26.750
I'll have to think about it.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:31.860
Your special day should be seen by as many people as possible...

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.160
That might be nice.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.160
Do think it over, won't you?

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:44.540
But if Papa finds out about this, I'm sure he'd be against it, so don't call me at home.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:46.500
I'll call you.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:50.670
Could you read her?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.640
It's not all that pretty...

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:56.640
All that's on her mind right now is to be in society's spotlight.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.950
She's not worried at all about his run-in with the law.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.750
She'll be trying on her dress at the chapel tomorrow.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.590
In a way, she's scarier than witches.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.230
The number you have dialed...

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.720
...is not in service.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.060
There's a reservation under her name, all right.

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:14.790
She forced them to hold it outside normal business hours.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.170
Tomorrow night, 2200 hours.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:19.810
Get ready.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:20.980
Okay.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.470
Um... What about me?

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.840
We'll have you earn your keep, naturally.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.290
I see... So that girl really was a hunter.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:44.330
My, my, we haven't seen you in a while, Miss Touko.

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.530
It's been a while, barkeep.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.730
Your usual? A sherry?

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:50.610
Please.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.570
Coming right up.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.480
Really, it has been a while...

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:31.910
You must be Mr. Misawa.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.470
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.850
You can wait here if you like, but since you're here, why not wait in the chapel?

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.420
I'll show you the way.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.790
Hey, would you like to try modeling my clothing line?

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:49.060
Hey, Kazuya, what do you...

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.960
Huh? Where did he go?

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.500
Geez, he pisses me off!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.900
I can't believe that guy!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.800
I'm on the second floor. Misawa isn't here.

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:04.170
He's in the chapel with one of the receptionists.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.010
Okay, got it.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.380
What do you think?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.040
Please, step up to the altar and take a good look around.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.510
Take your time, now.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:47.190
Wow, I even got to play dress-up today!

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.120
The ball's in your court now, guys.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:06.770
Misawa!

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:08.480
Dojima! Why weren't you on lookout?!

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.170
Wait.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.650
What, you again?

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.850
You hardly ever let me talk to you.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.490
Leave me alone! You'll hear from my lawyer if you keep bothering me!

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.430
That would be a problem.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:29.560
I'm in enough trouble as is. I lost my job because of you.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.260
But there's something that I just have to know.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.230
Just out of personal curiosity.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.340
I know it's not fair,

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:41.040
but that camera's going to be rolling to keep you from talking your way out again.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:42.640
He has a camera?

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:43.740
Amon, this is bad.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.480
Stay cool. We'll get our chance.

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:47.810
How did you kill him?

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:51.050
Understand, Misawa?! I don't buy that crap!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.320
I don't believe humans can have special powers!

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.850
Answer me! How did you kill him?!

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:57.550
Misawa!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.160
I've been trying to tell you that I didn't do anything.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.700
Oh, dear.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:11.670
This is big...

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:13.740
Oh, dear, would you look at this?

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.510
You're all my witnesses.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:21.250
I didn't do a thing, right? See, you even have it on tape...

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:25.680
I'm sorry, sir, but filming is not permitted inside the chapel.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.520
What're you doing, Dojima?!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.160
Hey, what's going on?

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:32.560
Who are you people?

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:47.170
You... You're doing this?

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.130
What are you doing?!

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:52.450
W-What right do you have...

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.820
Bastards!

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.020
Sakaki, that's enough.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:40.250
Karasuma, call the Factory.

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:43.760
W-What did you people do to me?

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:46.420
What happened to my powers?

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.490
Why are you doing this?!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.600
Because you're a witch.

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:14.600
You've withstood the sadness of your fiancée's mysterious disappearance...

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.860
...and have stepped in to take over his company.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:21.400
Yes, well, that's all that I have left of him now.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:23.770
Some reports say that he's dead.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:26.570
I have to believe that that's not true.

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.380
Inside my heart at least, he'll always...

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:44.950
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:47.810
Tell me.

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:59.800
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:09.690
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:14.180
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:19.550
...all those promises...

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:25.950
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:31.750
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:40.530
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
